**My Profile** in the drawer shows two things stacked: your **Account** — the username you sign in
with, and your **Teacher ID** — and your **Teacher Profile**, the record everything else keys off.

## Updating your details

1. Open **My Profile**.
2. Edit the fields under **Teacher Profile** — contact number, email, address and the rest.
3. Select **Save Changes**.

## Your photo

**Select Photo** uploads one; **Remove Photo** takes it off. This is the picture that appears next to
your name in class lists and staff directories.

## Changing your password

Under **Change Password**, enter the new password and confirm it, then select **Change Password**.

Do this the first time you sign in with a password an administrator gave you — a reset password is
displayed on screen to whoever performed the reset, so it should not stay in use.

## What you can't change here

Your **username** and **Teacher ID** are shown but not editable, and neither is the list of subjects
you teach — that one has real consequences, since it decides which classes you can be assigned to
and whether the timetable generator will ever schedule you. To change it, ask an administrator to
edit your record from **Teachers → Directory**.

